    "lines": [
     16,
     25
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies that {@link StringSubstitutor} can produce output that is textually identical to its input, even though a substitution genuinely occurs. <p>The {@code animal} variable expands to {@code \"$${${thing}}\"}; the leading {@code $$} is an escaped {@code $}, and {@code ${thing}} expands to {@code \"animal\"}. The net result of replacing {@code \"${animal}\"} is therefore the literal text {@code \"${animal}\"} again, so the whole template is replaced onto an identical string.</p>"
   },
   {
